{"title":"2021 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 20","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_OmegaLearn_(Using_parabola_properties_and_system_of_equations)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by OmegaLearn (Using parabola properties and system of equations)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_TheBeautyofMath\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by TheBeautyofMath</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#See_also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_20&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Suppose that on a parabola with vertex <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/2/d/12d58aa29201da09d8e620f8698e3a37547f6b4a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$V$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> and a focus <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/0/5/a055f405829e64a3b70253ab67cb45ed6ed5bb29.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$F$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> there exists a point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/6/f/d6fc95ce649c7f42e9a52546763ee1dbf684bb69.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AF=20$\" width=\"69\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/a/a/eaa44eb36d4a6061a593fb31c52508c7e4e356ad.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AV=21$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"69\" height=\"13\" />. What is the sum of all possible values of the length <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/f/d/dfd3b742254d53e1871a74e65b06b06d305d89d2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$FV?$\" width=\"37\" height=\"12\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/0/60043e0a55f5371e9930dde816d1104bd6bd1314.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A) }13 \\qquad \\textbf{(B) }\\frac{40}3 \\qquad \\textbf{(C) }\\frac{41}3 \\qquad \\textbf{(D) }14\\qquad \\textbf{(E) }\\frac{43}3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"409\" height=\"37\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_20&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/3/c/63c17c295325f731666c7d74952b563a01e00fcc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\ell$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"9\" height=\"14\" /> be the directrix of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/e/17e179805931e8a5004cd6ac6b3ad3a9b5020876.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\mathcal P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"14\" />; recall that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/e/17e179805931e8a5004cd6ac6b3ad3a9b5020876.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\mathcal P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"14\" /> is the set of points <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/5/5/2554b6496c3b678897e9b060ef00aa9f0a7d7ece.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$T$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> such that the distance from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/5/5/2554b6496c3b678897e9b060ef00aa9f0a7d7ece.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$T$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/3/c/63c17c295325f731666c7d74952b563a01e00fcc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\ell$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"9\" height=\"14\" /> is equal to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/2/5/c25436083d2a36da09136e1d9966e871ff0423f3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$TF$\" width=\"27\" height=\"12\" />. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/8/6/9866e3a998d628ba0941eb4fea0666ac391d149a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Q$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"16\" height=\"18\" /> be the orthogonal projections of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/0/5/a055f405829e64a3b70253ab67cb45ed6ed5bb29.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$F$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> onto <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/3/c/63c17c295325f731666c7d74952b563a01e00fcc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\ell$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"9\" height=\"14\" />, and further let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/4/6a47ca0fe7cb276abc022af6ac88ddae1a9d6894.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$X$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/e/5/ce58e4af225c93d08606c26554caaa5ae32edeba.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> be the orthogonal projections of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/0/5/a055f405829e64a3b70253ab67cb45ed6ed5bb29.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$F$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/2/d/12d58aa29201da09d8e620f8698e3a37547f6b4a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$V$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> onto <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/5/6/7563031eab26ad18658cf2f6a8e4948861bb9013.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AQ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"30\" height=\"18\" />. Because <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/5/2/4529a7feb059b07b78146d34a3024ffee8ddf79a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AF &lt; AV$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"79\" height=\"13\" />, there are two possible configurations which may arise, and they are shown below.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/9/bc94cb3aa05d8949f3622223c250dc10bd152d18.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] \timport olympiad; \tsize(230); defaultpen(linewidth(0.8)+fontsize(11pt)); real d = 1.1, edge = 2.5, Ax = 1.6; real f(real x) { return 1/(4*d) * x * x; } pair V = origin, F = (0,d), la = (-edge,-d), lb = (edge,-d), A = (Ax, f(Ax)); pair P = foot(F,la,lb), Q = foot(A,la,lb), X = foot(F,A,Q), Y = foot(V,A,Q); draw(P--F--A--V--Y^^F--X--Q^^rightanglemark(F,P,la,4)^^rightanglemark(A,Q,lb,4)^^rightanglemark(A,X,F,4)^^rightanglemark(A,Y,V,4),red); draw(graph(f,-2.5,2.5)); draw(la -- lb); dot(F^^A^^V); label(&quot;$F$&quot;,F,NW); label(&quot;$V$&quot;,V,SW); label(&quot;$A$&quot;,A,dir(F--A)); label(&quot;$P$&quot;,P,S,red); label(&quot;$Q$&quot;,Q,S,red); label(&quot;$X$&quot;,X,E,red); label(&quot;$Y$&quot;,Y,E,red); [/asy]\" width=\"385\" height=\"218\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/8/d/b8d2f8b78bd8f950d5ff6fb3ab95036ca940d10c.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] \timport olympiad; \tsize(200); defaultpen(linewidth(0.8)+fontsize(11pt)); real d = 0.7, edge = 2.5, Ax = 1.9; real f(real x) { return 1/(4*d) * x * x; } pair V = origin, F = (0,d), la = (-edge,-d), lb = (edge,-d), A = (Ax, f(Ax)); pair P = foot(F,la,lb), Q = foot(A,la,lb), X = foot(F,A,Q), Y = foot(V,A,Q); draw(Q--A--F--P^^F--X^^A--V--Y^^rightanglemark(F,P,la,4)^^rightanglemark(A,Q,lb,4)^^rightanglemark(A,X,F,4)^^rightanglemark(A,Y,V,4),red); draw(la -- lb); draw(graph(f,-2.5,2.5)); dot(F^^A^^V); label(&quot;$F$&quot;,F,NW); label(&quot;$V$&quot;,V,SW); label(&quot;$A$&quot;,A,dir(F--A)); label(&quot;$P$&quot;,P,S,red); label(&quot;$Q$&quot;,Q,S,red); label(&quot;$X$&quot;,X,E,red); label(&quot;$Y$&quot;,Y,E,red); [/asy]\" width=\"335\" height=\"222\" />\nSet <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/7/c/67cc95380e1eeb560ce11e4fb0a9cfdf45c172b2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d = FV$\" width=\"62\" height=\"12\" />, which by the definition of a parabola also equals <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/3/9/0397e5108d281f9136f1ae009b76d99bacd8ce71.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$VP$\" width=\"28\" height=\"12\" />. Then as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/7/fc7e92793a9ac53c34c65daed5934be9a4240fc2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AQ = AF = 20$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"122\" height=\"16\" />, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/5/3/a53d6d766d6419dc6d2b2e5cb3fc03f5c2e3d8d6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AY = 20 - d$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"104\" height=\"16\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/8/0987372755756c6ee15fe74124feca99eaba7b6f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AX = |20 - 2d|$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"121\" height=\"18\" />. Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/c/9/5c99a823846634597565041a563a2efb59baccd9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$FXYV$\" width=\"59\" height=\"12\" /> is a rectangle, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/4/f/64f75639cea423dc110b031ca27a050f4788305d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$FX = VY$\" width=\"83\" height=\"12\" />, so by Pythagorean Theorem on triangles <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/5/9/259bb6257a22298feaf00be011460470587deeb8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AFX$\" width=\"43\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/a/1/2a1261c78413cd8b4248120f1458a48c907f6b76.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AVY$\" width=\"42\" height=\"13\" />,\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/1/a/61a87ce497e756a48473054820b6e29e3b4ac1e5.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*} 21^2 - (20 - d)^2 &amp;= AV^2 - AY^2 = VY^2\\\\ &amp;= FX^2 = AF^2 - AX^2 = 20^2 - (20 - 2d)^2 \\end{align*}\" width=\"451\" height=\"47\" />\nThis equation simplifies to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/b/f/dbf35ca43b28f99c169558be3fa144300aedb41b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3d^2 - 40d + 41 = 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"149\" height=\"16\" />, which has solutions <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/f/57f4dbc54dddd61e8cf8c18f94c017a464f88ecf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d = \\tfrac{20\\pm\\sqrt{277}}3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -7px\" width=\"94\" height=\"26\" />. Both values of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/a/96ab646de7704969b91c76a214126b45f2b07b25.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> work - the smaller solution with the bottom configuration and the larger solution with the top configuration - and so the requested answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/f/9afa96edf985d9256f5d8d56e3ea1872c6206bd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(B)}\\ \\tfrac{40}{3}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"63\" height=\"32\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_20&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/4/f/74f4008768812f46db4b252c9e69cf98c5faaa4b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\mathcal{P}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> be the parabola, let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/2/d/12d58aa29201da09d8e620f8698e3a37547f6b4a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$V$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> be the origin, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/0/5/a055f405829e64a3b70253ab67cb45ed6ed5bb29.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$F$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> lie on the positive <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> axis, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/4/1/2415b0020fd3ac014cbbeafaea4f543837d36935.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d=FV$\" width=\"62\" height=\"12\" />. The equation of the parabola is then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/7/e/f7e5fb151d773127a88ac4d2e49a442431ef5435.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^{2}=4dy$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"69\" height=\"18\" />. If the coordinates of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/b/f3b4ea7280b88addac484cf73f439617a9498996.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(p, q),$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"44\" height=\"18\" /> then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/a/5/ba5f9ee97c29f2a36367ce5dd1c1c33a7ae3aaee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p^{2}+q^{2}=441$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"106\" height=\"18\" /> since the distance from the origin to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/2/5/f25d31faf472ddb4c698a14522fe8125c06f8dd8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$21$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />. Note also that the parabola is the set of all points equidistant from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/0/5/a055f405829e64a3b70253ab67cb45ed6ed5bb29.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$F$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> and a line known as its directrix, which in this case is a horizontal line <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/a/96ab646de7704969b91c76a214126b45f2b07b25.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> units below the origin. Since the distance from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> to its directrix is equal to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/b/a/cba4bccbcf02ccd89a4907b85c1b3a3e02c9a7cd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AF,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"30\" height=\"16\" /> then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/8/3/f8366cd6196dd8a9da6d38a3e9eafb109e99d53e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$20$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> units above this line and therefore <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/d/0/8d0e49ce313652c1203ffd89e42f0f514afcc0bd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$q=20-d$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"83\" height=\"16\" />. Substituting for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/f/36f73fc1312ee0349b3f3a0f3bd9eb5504339011.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/6/1/0615acc3725de21025457e7d6f7694dab8e2f758.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$q$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> yields <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/2/c/a2c892e99a873875055587a463b71e934e745e4b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4d(20-d)+(20-d)^{2}=441$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"230\" height=\"21\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/5/a/85a303b607c4b00292180c7653428a7ac3980d79.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(20-d)(20+3d)=441,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"192\" height=\"18\" /> which simplifies to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/f/c3fd90368167d64c593ff893ccb2fb2280515b77.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3d^{2}-40d+41=0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"149\" height=\"16\" />. Therefore the sum of all possible values of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/a/96ab646de7704969b91c76a214126b45f2b07b25.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/a/8ca2c31ed6616e55fd8ec47ca4d132efc93f5ed1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\tfrac{-b}{a}=\\boxed{\\textbf{(B)} ~\\tfrac{40}{3}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"107\" height=\"32\" /> by Viète's Formulas.\n</p><p>~sugar_rush\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3\">Solution 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_20&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Two possible cases for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> exist, either, it lies on the latus rectum endpoints, in which <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/d/1/0d1ab5b1df22bba5a228a55790d9ecdf1a3e43c6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$VF = 10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"73\" height=\"14\" />, or it doesn't, in which <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/b/e/3beab97faa34953d81ec883718a24aa0501814fb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$VF = 20-x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"106\" height=\"16\" /> where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/7/7/877839d2f2ed062cf6d2bda204bfeb2a4153b2dc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A(x,y)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"58\" height=\"20\" />. The first case is not allowed as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/d/3/0d3cf577ea9b247ffa9c36a86fa4dfa55e407262.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AF = 21$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"72\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/d/1/0d1ab5b1df22bba5a228a55790d9ecdf1a3e43c6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$VF = 10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"73\" height=\"14\" /> forces <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/8/e/68edc676b83d669ae2b62876a52c7543462f30da.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$FA \\neq 20$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"72\" height=\"18\" />. Therefore, the second case must be true.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/8/7/087b704c188e27a72d373ba72010e77f751e4d00.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] size(8cm);  // Configuration parameters for a standard parabola setup real p = 13/3; pair V = (0,0); pair F = (p, 0);  // Coordinates for point A (not on the latus rectum) real x = 20 - p; real y = sqrt(4 * p * x); pair A = (x, y);  // Draw the parabola curve path parab = (0,0); for(real t=0.1; t&lt;=2.5; t+=0.1) {     parab = parab--(t*t*p, 2*p*t); } draw(parab, blue+1pt);  // Draw the axis of symmetry draw((-2,0)--(25,0), gray+dashed);  // Draw segments from A to Vertex and Focus draw(V--A, black); draw(F--A, black);  // Label key points dot(&quot;$V$&quot;, V, SW); dot(&quot;$F$&quot;, F, S); dot(&quot;$A$&quot;, A, NE); [/asy]\" width=\"378\" height=\"315\" />\n</p><p>Suppose <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/7/7/877839d2f2ed062cf6d2bda204bfeb2a4153b2dc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A(x,y)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"58\" height=\"20\" />. Then, if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/2/d/12d58aa29201da09d8e620f8698e3a37547f6b4a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$V$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/6/f9603ca3089464e548fc6f1366bc474e7efef8d9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(0,0)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"42\" height=\"20\" /> for instance it follows <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/6/516ec0f4c1fe5220d3069daa0f795c7e3e618e87.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$F(0,p)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"57\" height=\"20\" /> for some <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/f/36f73fc1312ee0349b3f3a0f3bd9eb5504339011.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" />. Also, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/6/7/66715785ccffda046dcc1e5cef475883c618e685.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^2 + y^2 = 441$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"110\" height=\"20\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/c/3/cc3e1cb37b24e355aeb2980e5c9a09f60b903313.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^2 + (y-p)^2 = 400$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"156\" height=\"21\" />. Finally, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/7/8c76df54c3d8e1c47ee9aa1cb0c440f5e4a7c8e3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^2 = 4py$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"72\" height=\"20\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/c/0/2c018fee689c694fbaa3fe29ca09ca2cb2e5363a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{x^2}{4p} = y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"58\" height=\"44\" />. Solving for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/f/36f73fc1312ee0349b3f3a0f3bd9eb5504339011.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" />, one could obtain the quartic <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/7/a/a7a9b4b758bdd4d7190906458d7faba6bef190aa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$9p^4 -1354p^2 +1681 = 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"195\" height=\"20\" />, which solves nicely as\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/5/1/651c0c49a9a1ab0ddf12d9af4734bb8bd05326e3.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[p = \\frac{\\pm 20 \\pm \\sqrt{277}}{3}\\]\" width=\"133\" height=\"41\" />\n</p><p>The only two positive solutions (as distance is never negative) is \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/7/8/a7812c76593e0e6192ff10b821f1b9e79283fd12.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[p = \\frac{20 \\pm \\sqrt{277}}{3}\\]\" width=\"119\" height=\"41\" />, \nwhose sum is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/f/c/1fc734aff36c6855f14589b0d07bd3237c340c02.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\frac{40}{3}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -19px\" width=\"35\" height=\"49\" />.\n</p><p>~Pinotation\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Video_Solution_by_OmegaLearn_.28Using_parabola_properties_and_system_of_equations.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_OmegaLearn_(Using_parabola_properties_and_system_of_equations)\">Video Solution by OmegaLearn (Using parabola properties and system of equations)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_20&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by OmegaLearn (Using parabola properties and system of equations)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/DcaD9vvcKL0\">https://youtu.be/DcaD9vvcKL0</a>\n</p><p>~ pi_is_3.14\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_TheBeautyofMath\">Video Solution by TheBeautyofMath</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_20&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by TheBeautyofMath\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/WidS_IOjkQo\">https://youtu.be/WidS_IOjkQo</a>\n</p><p>~IceMatrix\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_20&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"2\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_AMC_12A\" title=\"2021 AMC 12A\">2021 AMC 12A</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_AMC_12A_Problems\" title=\"2021 AMC 12A Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?tit